EU Artificial Intelligence Act catalog
=======================================

Source
------
Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 of the European Parliament and of the Council of
13 June 2024 laying down harmonised rules on artificial intelligence (Artificial
Intelligence Act), OJ L, 12.7.2024.
ELI: http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1689/oj

Copyright / licensing status
----------------------------
The official text of EU legislation published in the Official Journal of the
European Union may be freely reused, including for commercial purposes, under
Commission Decision 2011/833/EU on the reuse of Commission documents, provided
the source is acknowledged and the meaning is not distorted. Unlike copyrighted
standards (e.g. ISO/IEC 42001), the normative text of the AI Act could therefore
be quoted verbatim.

What this catalog contains
--------------------------
- The AI Act's article and Annex IDENTIFIERS (e.g. Article 5, Article 9–17,
  Article 27/50/53/55/72/73, Annex III points 1–8). These are the Regulation's
  own references.
- ORIGINAL one-line summaries and descriptions authored for this project. They
  paraphrase the intent of each provision; they are NOT verbatim AI Act text.
- The risk-tier model the AI Act establishes: prohibited practices (Art. 5),
  high-risk systems (Art. 6 + Annex I / Annex III), transparency-risk systems
  (Art. 50), and general-purpose AI models incl. systemic risk (Art. 51–55).

Even though the AI Act text is freely reusable and could be quoted directly, we
use our own wording so the catalog stays consistent in tone and length with the
other framework catalogs in this repository.

Attribution
-----------
Where this catalog is surfaced to users, attribute the source as:
"Based on Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 (EU Artificial Intelligence Act),
OJ L, 12.7.2024 — © European Union, http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1689/oj"
